 "title": "Lipid Production in Yeast and Fungi",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around lipid production in yeast and fungi, with a focus on Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Candida curvatus. S. cerevisiae has a major role in lipid production and has been engineered to express various genes, including amdS, which is similar to Aspergillus nidulans. C. curvatus has been used for FTIR microspectroscopy and has spectral features of linolenic acid and palmitoleic acid. The cluster also includes various genes and proteins involved in lipid production, such as PDC1 and PDC2, as well as fatty acids and other chemicals related to lipid production.",
